1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,880
 - How was it? - Great!

2
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:03,720
 (screams)

3
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:05,800
 - Did you make any friends? - Yes.

4
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:06,960
 - What are their names? Tell me.

5
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:07,840
 Tell me everything about your day.

6
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:08,760
 I want to know it all.

7
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:10,760
 - Can I have like a little quiet time?

8
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,160
 - Sure. Yes.

9
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:15,000
 Sorry.

10
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,620
 Shut up, mom!

11
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:21,040
 Silence from you!

12
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:22,560
 - This is not quiet time.

13
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:23,400
 - Okay.

14
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,200
 - Okay, most kids are not able to articulately

15
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,760
 and respectfully voice their need for quiet time,

16
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:31,560
 but it is what most kids want after school.

17
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:32,680
 Think about it this way for you.

18
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:34,760
 Let's say you have your first day in the office

19
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:36,720
 or maybe it's the second week.

20
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:38,280
 You're managing everyone's names.

21
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:39,620
 You're going from meeting to meeting.

22
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:40,800
 You have a new presentation.

23
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:43,120
 You're making conversation with people at lunch.

24
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:44,980
 And then you finally get home to a roommate,

25
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:46,800
 to a partner, and the questions begin.

26
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:47,800
 Hey, how was work?

27
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:49,240
 Okay, tell me who your new best friend is.

28
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:50,240
 Okay, who do you have lunch with?

29
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:51,080
 Who do you sit with?

30
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:52,000
 Anything challenge today?

31
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,360
 Anything surprising today?

32
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,640
 Anything that you did that you thought you couldn't do?

33
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:57,260
 All amazing questions.

34
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:58,600
 It's just that the timing is off.

35
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,140
 You probably worked hard to hold it together at work all day.

36
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:03,440
 You looked fine on the outside,

37
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:05,120
 but there was a lot going on on the inside.

38
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:07,280
 You now just need to decompress,

39
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:10,100
 probably around someone who knows and loves you,

40
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:13,000
 but you need that person to not have such an agenda,

41
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,500
 to not put a demand on you to answer questions.

42
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:18,000
 So just hold your questions.

43
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,320
 Wait 20 minutes, 40 minutes, if you can, 60 minutes.

44
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:24,320
 I promise you it will work out better for both of you.

